    <!-- The Dokka HTML for `serverpackcreator-api` is NOT a Writerside topic and cannot be one. Writerside
         has no way to host a generated file tree: `cfg/static` takes individually *referenced* files only
         (see build-profiles.xsd), and JetBrains' own WRS-1772 "Integration with Dokka" is still open. The two
         outputs are therefore merged at PACKAGING time, in two places that must stay in step.
         `docker/Dockerfile.help` copies Dokka to `/config/www/api/`, and `.github/workflows/pages.yml`
         assembles the same layout for GitHub Pages.

         THE HREF MUST BE AN ABSOLUTE URL, and a relative one is not a smaller version of that — it does not
         navigate at all. The published help is a single-page app, and its viewer treats a link as a real
         anchor only when the target carries a scheme: the check is `isExternal || /^(?:[a-z]+:)?\/\//`
         against the href. Anything else becomes a client-side route, so `api/index.html` leaves the Dokka
         tree untouched on disk and instead pushes the URL to `/api/`, where the app re-bootstraps and asks
         for `api/config.json`, `api/HelpTOC.json` and `api/api-object-digest.json`. Those are Writerside's
         own files and exist only at the site root, so all three answer 404 and the page dies on
         "TOC data error". A root-absolute `/.../api/index.html` fails the same test — one leading slash is
         not two — so it is no answer either. Nor is there an author-settable escape: the builder derives
         `data-external="true"` from the href being absolute, and `topic.v2.xsd` has no attribute for it.
         Typing the Dokka URL directly always works; it is only the click that does not.

         The cost of being absolute is that this one link leaves a self-hosted container for the public site.
         It is the only shape the viewer will navigate, and a container still serves its own copy at `/api/`
         for anyone who addresses it directly.
         (Note for editors: an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen anywhere, which is why this block
         uses none.) -->
    <toc-element toc-title="Kotlin API (Dokka)" href="https://griefed.github.io/ServerPackCreator/api/index.html"/>
